{"id":"2b89fe09-2476-423c-94ac-9876f561eb7b","object":"chat.completion","created":1785018154,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case or \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing threshold or calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be number\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be list\\\")\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call must be dict\\\")\\n        if not all(k in call for k in (\\\"call_id\\\",\\\"loss_without_call\\\",\\\"loss_with_call\\\",\\\"prediction_tokens\\\",\\\"parseable\\\")):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call missing required fields\\\")\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be boolean\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        accepted = (parseable == True) and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the task: \"Implement api_call_loss_filter through solve(case)\". The case payload has \"threshold\" and \"calls\" (list of objects with call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable). The output schema: accepted_call_ids (list of strings), diagnostics (list of objects with accepted (bool), call_id (str), normalized_gain (number)). The mechanism:\n\nFor each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (at least one token, so denominator is prediction_tokens). Then check if parseable is true AND normalized_gain >= threshold. If so, accept. The normalized_gain should be rounded? The specification says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Probably round normalized_gain to some reasonable number of decimal places? But the schema says type: number, not integer. The fixtures show values like 0.30132987 etc. The gain is difference of floats. We need to compute normalized_gain as a float. Rounding is not specified exactly; maybe to avoid floating point issues, but the input numbers have high precision. The instruction says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Could be rounding to something like 8 decimal places? But we can just keep the float as computed. However, the output in fixtures? We don't have outputs. We can compute and output the float exactly. The schema says \"normalized_gain\" is number, not integer. So we can just return the computed float.\n\nImportant: Keep diagnostics in supplied call order. So iterate over calls in the order