ce(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be list\")\n    \n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"call must be dict\")\n        if not all(k in call for k in (\"call_id\",\"loss_without_call\",\"loss_with_call\",\"prediction_tokens\",\"parseable\")):\n            raise ValueError(\"call missing required fields\")\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int,float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_without_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int,float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_with_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be boolean\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        accepted = (parseable == True) and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nWe need to ensure the returned values are JSON-serializable. The floats are fine.\n\nAlso note the output schema requires additionalProperties false at both levels. Our dicts only have those keys.\n\nNow embed as JSON string. The final answer must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\". The value is a string containing the Python source code. We need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes appropriately.\n\nLet's write the source code as a multi-line string, then escape for JSON.\n\nI'll produce the final JSON.\n\nBut careful: The task says \"Return one JSON object with exactly one key, implementation.\" So the response should be like {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}.\n\nWe must not include any other text. No code fences.\n\nI'll now produce the JSON string."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1809,"total_tokens":3973,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1270},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}